{
  "$schema": "./SCHEMA.md#identity-created-signing",
  "description": "identity.created v2 signing bytes (avalon_protocol::identity_id::identity_created_signing_bytes_v2): UTF-8 of 'avalon:identity.created:v2:{len(network_id)}:{network_id}:{len(shard_id)}:{shard_id}:{ticket_id}:{identity_id}:{public_key_hex}:{display_name}', where len is the decimal UTF-8 byte length (network and shard ids are variable-width and shard ids contain ':', so each is length-prefixed). ticket_id is the server-issued register/start ticket, network_id the ledger network and shard_id the shard the entry is issued in, so a copied signature does not verify for another ticket, network or shard (replayVectors). The display name is last, so a ':' in it is harmless; it is taken as-is (multi-byte UTF-8 stays UTF-8, no normalisation). The public key is lowercase HEX in the signing bytes and standard BASE64 on the wire. The signature is Ed25519 by the identity's inception key over the bytes (verified strictly).",
